hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17612","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ziyad ibn Labid, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned something and said: And that will be at the time when knowledge departs. We said: O Messenger of Allah, how will knowledge depart when we recite the Qur'an and teach it to our sons, and our sons will teach it to their sons until the Day of Resurrection? He said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O son of Umm Labid, I used to see you among the most understanding men in Madinah. Are not these Jews and Christians reciting the Torah and the Gospel without benefiting from what is in them at all?"
